{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1128633-do-members-of-house-merinita-retain-their-memories-post-enchantment","id":1128633,"title":"Do members of House Merinita retain their memories post Enchantment?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-13T17:27:26-07:00","id":1128633,"title":"Do members of House Merinita retain their memories post Enchantment?","content":"The Hollow One book states that the Tradition is unique in that they can retain their memories of the Dreaming rather than lose them to the Mists due to their paradigm being so attuned to the Dreaming. Should I assume House Merinita which specializes in Fair Folk study and power over the Dreaming is similarly unaffected by the Mists?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T17:51:47-07:00","id":1128644,"title":"","content":"I should certainly think so. They are literally the wizards who specialize in fae matters. It would be nonsensical for them not to have figured out how Enchantment and such works, and learned how to game that system.<br /> <br /> Personally, I don't see why Mages shouldn't be able to see Chimerical reality with the right Mind rotes. The Spheres can theoretically do anything, after all. If anyone knows the rotes in question, it would be 1) House Merinita, 2) the Verbana, 3) certain specialist Dreamspeakers, and 4) the aforementioned Hollow Ones. It shouldn't be exclusive knowledge, just rare and specialized.<br /> <br /> Moreover, House Merinita probably has a high concentration of Fae-blooded members. If the Order of Hermes finds a recruit who sees chimerical reality, they forward them to House Merinita. Just seems intuitive, right? Like, are you really going to waste such an initiate on any other House, when Merinita is the one most likely to put the initiate's abilities to good use? And are the most likely to help them handle their natural perceptions of a level of reality that is esoteric even by Hermetic standards? Having the fae-blooded person join other Houses is just asking for trouble. The Order has rules against entanglements with the Kindly Ones for a reason (excluding Merinita, obviously).<br /> <br /> The rotes I mentioned earlier are mainly for members of House Merinita that don't happen to have fae blood, or for casting on other mages when necessary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T18:15:44-07:00","id":1128653,"title":"","content":"I'd be reading up on the older Ars Magica works for how Merinita deals with Fae. That being said, they are the Order of Hermes experts on the fae, so they probably know how to not completely forget what happens in fae lands.<br /> <br /> The corebook for Ars Magica 4th edition (one edition before the present one) is a free download on Steve Jackson Games' webstore, warehouse 23<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.warehouse23.com/products/ars-magica-4th-edition-core-rulebook\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.warehouse23.com/products/ars-magica-4th-edition-core-rulebook\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.warehouse23.com/products/ars-magica-4th-edition-core-rulebook\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.warehouse23.com/products/ars-magica-4th-edition-core-rulebook </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T17:44:52-07:00","id":1130058,"title":"","content":"Good answers. I really wish Merinita got fleshed out more, but I guess this is where i have to use my imagination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T19:13:45-07:00","id":1130083,"title":"","content":"You can certainly go to Ars Magica for more Merinita ideas. Even the fifth edition of Ars Magica, the current edition, has the Merinita in a book. That would be <i>Houses of Hermes: Mystery Cults. </i>Of course the systems are different, so even if you're mining for ideas, you have to use your imagination to switch between the High Mythic Age in a world primarily about Hermetics and the setting of your Mage: the Ascension chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T22:12:19-07:00","id":1130143,"title":"","content":"Agreed with the above. I've recently read through Houses of Hermes: Mystery Cults, and found it informative for House Meritina. That said, it does indeed require a bit of work to translate.<br /> <br /> Merinita isn't nearly as big as it was in the Dark Ages - it WAS demoted from a major House, after all - and many of the political and ideological divisions described in the book (if they apply at all to the World of Darkness) are dated and likely of little consequence. When there are barely any Merinita left, factions either blend together or are made up by individual cabals (or even individuals).<br /> <br /> Probably the biggest difference between ArM and MtAs, when it comes to House Merinita, is the nature of their subject of interest: the Fae. Note how denizens of the Dreaming differ from the inhabitants of the Faerie Realm in ArM. And always remember that, while in Mythic Europe the Fae are a potent (if waning) force, in the World of Darkness they barely have a presence in the material world. The diminished role of fairies and Changelings matches the diminished potency of House Merinita, so adjust accordingly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T05:45:41-07:00","id":1130216,"title":"","content":"N/A........","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 08-17-2017, 02:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T06:09:57-07:00","id":1130223,"title":"","content":"I wonder if it is a chicken and egg situation. Merinita is shrinking because of the decreases power of the Dreaming but the Dreaming is whithering in part because of lack of interest by the magi. If Merinita could drum up more mages to join them in learning the power of the Dreaming the Dreaming might grow in power and the Fae in numbers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T06:26:10-07:00","id":1130228,"title":"","content":"Well, Changeling fans may not like mages being that important...but it's an interesting way to see things from the perspective of a character of that house. Making Changelings Great Again may as well be the long therm goal for a Merinita character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T11:52:23-07:00","id":1130383,"title":"","content":"It is written in Changeling source material that the Changelings (notably the Sidhe) are monitoring/learning about the Hidden Ones/Lords of Order (aka the Technocracy). It is difficult for Changelings because Technocrats and Technocratic places tend to be super banal.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I imagine most Technocrats are fairly blind to chimerical reality. Although Technocrats likely would register most Changelings as Reality Deviants fairly easily, I'm not sure the Technocracy would have much insight into the world of Changelings/the Fae.<br /> <br /> The Changeling source material does suggest that Changelings tend to have more information about the Hidden Ones than the Hidden Ones do about Changelings or the Fae.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy's vision for the world does not, on the whole, seem helpful to Changelings/the Dreaming. To some extent, Changelings and Tradition Mages have common aims.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12988-imperator","name":"Imperator","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T15:42:35-07:00","id":1130992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1128633-do-members-of-house-merinita-retain-their-memories-post-enchantment?p=1130228#post1130228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, Changeling fans may not like mages being that important...but it's an interesting way to see things from the perspective of a character of that house. Making Changelings Great Again may as well be the long therm goal for a Merinita character.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm thinking of one who has the Shaman merit and has Dana as his totem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}